# Every Dockerfile here builds with the repo root as its context (see the
# header comment in worker/Dockerfile) and COPYs the two or three directories
# it actually needs. Without this file the daemon still uploads the whole
# repo — including node_modules, which CI materializes *before* the image
# build: docker.yml runs `bun install --frozen-lockfile && bun test` in the
# same workspace it then builds from.
#
# Only entries nothing COPYs. Check `grep '^COPY' */Dockerfile` before adding
# to this list — dashboard/ is copied wholesale by core/Dockerfile, so its
# sources must not appear here, only its build outputs.

.git
.github
.claude
.mcp.json

# Dependencies and build outputs — every image installs/builds its own.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dashboard/dist
core/internal/webui/dist

# Docs and prose. Nothing is COPYed from these.
docs
*.md

# The disposable kind cluster's manifests (local/kind/), and the deploy
# manifests ArgoCD reads straight from git.
local
k8s

# Cloned by the provisioner at runtime from git (docs/adr/0032), never baked
# into an image.
fleet-shared

# Test and tooling noise.
**/*_test.go
**/.DS_Store
**/coverage
